Go.

1202
00:39:14,040 --> 00:39:15,040
Next.

1203
00:39:16,080 --> 00:39:17,080
Three, two, one.

1204
00:39:17,340 --> 00:39:18,340
OK.

1205
00:39:19,040 --> 00:39:20,720
We're in sync.

1206
00:39:21,640 --> 00:39:23,719
Very fast, we can get four balls now.

1207
00:39:23,720 --> 00:39:25,120
Here we go.

1208
00:39:26,580 --> 00:39:27,979
How many seconds?

1209
00:39:27,980 --> 00:39:29,060
Seventeen.

1210
00:39:30,080 --> 00:39:31,559
Go.

1211
00:39:31,560 --> 00:39:32,520
We got it!

1212
00:39:32,520 --> 00:39:33,520
Bring in the eggplant.

1213
00:39:33,920 --> 00:39:34,500
And beef.

1214
00:39:34,500 --> 00:39:35,000
You go in first.

1215
00:39:35,001 --> 00:39:36,460
You go first, you take two things.

1216
00:39:39,960 --> 00:39:42,139
Ingredients are here.

1217
00:39:42,140 --> 00:39:44,339
Shrimp, mushrooms, onion, ginger, garlic

1218
00:39:44,340 --> 00:39:46,199
and green peppers

1219
00:39:46,200 --> 00:39:47,600
and beef.

1220
00:39:48,800 --> 00:39:49,839
Thanks, good work.

1221
00:39:49,840 --> 00:39:51,399
Take a rest.

1222
00:39:51,400 --> 00:39:53,400
I'll start cooking dinner.

1223
00:39:53,820 --> 00:39:56,379
Come on, wash the veggies.

1224
00:39:56,380 --> 00:39:57,880
I'll wash outside.

1225
00:40:02,160 --> 00:40:02,860
You just got back.

1226
00:40:02,860 --> 00:40:03,660
Go rest outside,

1227
00:40:03,660 --> 00:40:04,660
we'll handle it.

1228
00:40:05,360 --> 00:40:06,460
Really?

1229
00:40:07,680 --> 00:40:09,019
Yes, go rest.

1230
00:40:09,020 --> 00:40:10,940
You eat pork and beef?

1231
00:40:10,965 --> 00:40:11,900
Quietly getting to work.

1232
00:40:12,100 --> 00:40:13,699
Already eaten

1233
00:40:13,700 --> 00:40:14,939
I think it'll be tasty.

1234
00:40:14,940 --> 00:40:16,299
There are six

1235
00:40:16,300 --> 00:40:17,939
I'll help wash outside

1236
00:40:17,940 --> 00:40:19,140
I'll go wash outside.

1237
00:40:20,760 --> 00:40:22,300
Let me help you wash.

1238
00:40:32,940 --> 00:40:34,579
Need all of them washed?

1239
00:40:34,580 --> 00:40:35,580
I think enough

1240
00:40:35,780 --> 00:40:37,520
six eggplants.

1241
00:40:38,080 --> 00:40:39,620
And they said tomato scrambled eggs.

1242
00:40:40,320 --> 00:40:41,779
Tomato scrambled eggs?

1243
00:40:41,780 --> 00:40:42,560
Need peppers?

1244
00:40:42,561 --> 00:40:45,059
But why isn't the tomato washed?

1245
00:40:45,060 --> 00:40:46,060
Where's the tomato?

1246
00:40:46,061 --> 00:40:47,959
I'll get the tomato.

1247
00:40:47,960 --> 00:40:49,519
I said tomato scrambled eggs.

1248
00:40:49,520 --> 00:40:51,020
Why is there no tomato?

1249
00:40:51,700 --> 00:40:54,200
(The tomato is here)

1250
00:40:58,020 --> 00:40:58,720
Tomato is here.

1251
00:40:58,720 --> 00:40:59,320
Here it is.

1252
00:40:59,320 --> 00:41:00,320
I'll take them all.

1253
00:41:00,680 --> 00:41:01,480
Are you done washing?

1254
00:41:01,480 --> 00:41:02,160
Washed?

1255
00:41:02,161 --> 00:41:03,359
Yes.

1256
00:41:03,360 --> 00:41:03,980
You need tomatoes?

1257
00:41:03,980 --> 00:41:04,800
No.

1258
00:41:04,801 --> 00:41:06,499
They said they need tomatoes.

1259
00:41:06,522 --> 00:41:08,062
We're outside, we didn’t wash them yet.

1260
00:41:09,900 --> 00:41:10,900
He seems to need...

1261
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:21,300
Who wants garlic?

1262
00:41:21,301 --> 00:41:22,999
Get a big plate.

1263
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:23,760
Garlic?

1264
00:41:23,761 --> 00:41:24,799
Garlic, yes.

1265
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:25,400
How many?

1266
00:41:25,401 --> 00:41:27,339
Can you peel two?

1267
00:41:27,340 --> 00:41:29,399
I want garlic too.

1268
00:41:29,400 --> 00:41:30,839
Want garlic, right?

1269
00:41:30,840 --> 00:41:32,639
I need!

1270
00:41:32,640 --> 00:41:34,039
Just peel one

1271
00:41:34,040 --> 00:41:34,740
one whole bulb.

1272
00:41:34,741 --> 00:41:36,080
Then chop it.

1273
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:40,219
They want garlic.

1274
00:41:40,220 --> 00:41:42,239
You wash，I'll peel garlic.

1275
00:41:42,240 --> 00:41:42,920
OK.

1276
00:41:42,921 --> 00:41:44,039
Yes，I'll go peel garlic.

1277
00:41:44,040 --> 00:41:44,820
I'll peel the garlic.

1278
00:41:44,820 --> 00:41:45,820
How many does he want?

1279
00:41:46,220 --> 00:41:47,220
One whole bulb.

1280
00:41:47,460 --> 00:41:48,020
One whole?

1281
00:41:48,020 --> 00:41:49,020
All of it.

1282
00:42:01,760 --> 00:42:03,019
Do you use peppers?

1283
00:42:03,020 --> 00:42:03,820
Peppers?

1284
00:42:03,820 --> 00:42:04,560
He does.

1285
00:42:04,560 --> 00:42:05,560
I don't.

1286
00:42:13,300 --> 00:42:14,599
Honestly

1287
00:42:14,600 --> 00:42:16,939
I don't know what to talk about

1288
00:42:16,940 --> 00:42:18,840
so I'll just do practical things.

1289
00:42:19,240 --> 00:42:19,840
There's no minced pork.

1290
00:42:19,841 --> 00:42:21,059
I'll make noise.

1291
00:42:21,060 --> 00:42:22,060
Sorry, teachers.

1292
00:42:22,800 --> 00:42:24,779
Are you really chopping it by hand?

1293
00:42:24,780 --> 00:42:26,580
Yes, there's no minced meat.

1294
00:42:27,300 --> 00:42:28,840
There's no minced meat.

1295
00:42:32,640 --> 00:42:33,440
We're going to be sued.

1296
00:42:33,441 --> 00:42:34,659
You need minced meat?

1297
00:42:34,660 --> 00:42:37,059
Is there? Yes.

1298
00:42:37,060 --> 00:42:39,100
Really? Then what am I chopping?

1299
00:42:41,260 --> 00:42:43,280
Yes, it is.

1300
00:42:43,304 --> 00:42:44,616
(right-hand man)

1301
00:42:44,640 --> 00:42:45,640
Fine.

1302
00:42:48,720 --> 00:42:49,620
Is this minced meat?

1303
00:42:49,621 --> 00:42:51,119
Yes, it is.

1304
00:42:51,120 --> 00:42:52,559
Waner

1305
00:42:52,560 --> 00:42:53,579
he is very quiet,

1306
00:42:53,580 --> 00:42:54,979
but while we were cooking

1307
00:42:54,980 --> 00:42:55,980
he came over to ask me

1308
00:42:55,981 --> 00:42:57,419
if I needed help.

1309
00:42:57,420 --> 00:42:58,959
And then each time

1310
00:42:58,960 --> 00:42:59,999
after washing things

1311
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:01,059
he asked me

1312
00:43:01,060 --> 00:43:02,799
if he can help me.

1313
00:43:02,800 --> 00:43:04,200
That's nice.

1314
00:43:06,300 --> 00:43:11,300
(Today's Chef)

1315
00:43:24,740 --> 00:43:25,820
You're washing outside.

1316
00:43:26,880 --> 00:43:28,739
Are these washed?

1317
00:43:28,740 --> 00:43:29,919
Yes, wait, I'll finish.

1318
00:43:29,920 --> 00:43:32,120
I'll bring them in.

1319
00:43:40,900 --> 00:43:41,600
This is Shanghai bok choy.

1320
00:43:41,601 --> 00:43:42,819
Not washed yet.

1321
00:43:42,820 --> 00:43:43,820
Not washed.

1322
00:43:48,800 --> 00:43:49,500
We have mushrooms.

1323
00:43:49,501 --> 00:43:51,099
There's more outside.

1324
00:43:51,100 --> 00:43:52,040
How do you want to cook this?

1325
00:43:52,041 --> 00:43:53,139
I think...

1326
00:43:53,140 --> 00:43:54,000
Stir‑fry with beef?

1327
00:43:54,001 --> 00:43:55,899
I think that works.

1328
00:43:55,900 --> 00:43:57,079
It’s really possible.

1329
00:43:57,080 --> 00:43:58,080
It's fine.

1330
00:43:59,040 --> 00:43:59,520
Old Xu.

1331
00:43:59,520 --> 00:44:00,280
After you're done

1332
00:44:00,281 --> 00:44:01,619
grab me a bowl.

1333
00:44:01,620 --> 00:44:02,160
Can you get me a bowl?

1334
00:44:02,160 --> 00:44:02,880
Sure.

1335
00:44:02,881 --> 00:44:04,779
How did you become "Old"?

1336
00:44:04,780 --> 00:44:05,780
Just rinse it.

1337
00:44:07,180 --> 00:44:08,779
Weren't you "Xiao" (young) just now?

1338
00:44:08,780 --> 00:44:09,180
Yes.

1339
00:44:09,180 --> 00:44:10,120
This morning you were Young

1340
00:44:10,120 --> 00:44:11,120
now you're Old Xu.

1341
00:44:12,020 --> 00:44:13,020
It's fine.

1342
00:44:14,380 --> 00:44:15,659
Elio.

1343
00:44:15,660 --> 00:44:16,859
Quite warm.

1344
00:44:16,860 --> 00:44:17,760
I feel he's...

1345
00:44:17,761 --> 00:44:19,159
actually a little like me

1346
00:44:19,160 --> 00:44:20,660
I've got a good impression of him.

1347
00:44:21,500 --> 00:44:22,759
Let's see if you've finished.

1348
00:44:22,760 --> 00:44:23,560
Yes, waiting for him.

1349
00:44:23,561 --> 00:44:24,659
OK.

1350
00:44:24,660 --> 00:44:25,620
You're going to stir‑fry the beef?

1351
00:44:25,643 --> 00:44:26,662
Beef is a must.

1352
00:44:27,460 --> 00:44:29,300
I really want beef.

1353
00:44:29,900 --> 00:44:31,519
We played so hard today,

1354
00:44:31,520 --> 00:44:33,439
just to get beef.

1355
00:44:33,440 --> 00:44:35,099
Stir‑fry beef.

1356
00:44:35,100 --> 00:44:36,399
If we don't eat it,

1357
00:44:36,400 --> 00:44:37,400
my heart will break.

1358
00:44:40,920 --> 00:44:42,539
"Spring and autumn pass

1359
00:44:42,540 --> 00:44:45,440
but this love never ends."

1360
00:45:00,600 --> 00:45:02,439
During summer breaks

1361
00:45:02,440 --> 00:45:05,499
I had vacations

1362
00:45:05,500 --> 00:45:06,779
I wanted to go out

1363
00:45:06,780 --> 00:45:08,179
and see life.

1364
00:45:08,180 --> 00:45:09,940
It was my first time learning to

1365
00:45:10,640 --> 00:45:12,239
cook at a restaurant.

1366
00:45:12,240 --> 00:45:14,519
I tried it.

1367
00:45:14,520 --> 00:45:16,019
I worked there about

1368
00:45:16,020 --> 00:45:17,639
half a month, it was tiring

1369
00:45:17,640 --> 00:45:19,220
but I learned to cook.

1370
00:45:21,280 --> 00:45:22,379
What are you washing?

1371
00:45:22,380 --> 00:45:23,680
Lettuce.

1372
00:45:25,020 --> 00:45:26,300
Here you go.

1373
00:45:28,020 --> 00:45:29,100
Can you wash shrimp?

1374
00:45:30,100 --> 00:45:31,259
Shrimp?

1375
00:45:31,260 --> 00:45:32,539
I think you don't need to wash

1376
00:45:32,540 --> 00:45:33,759
just blanch them

1377
00:45:33,760 --> 00:45:35,040
just blanch in water.

1378
00:45:37,440 --> 00:45:39,699
Who's eating this? You're eating it?

1379
00:45:39,700 --> 00:45:40,979
You're adding extra food for yourself?

1380
00:45:40,980 --> 00:45:42,139
I'm too hungry.

1381
00:45:42,140 --> 00:45:43,400
I'll eat a raw tomato.

1382
00:45:51,240 --> 00:45:52,419
How do you wash this?

1383
00:45:52,420 --> 00:45:54,039
Tear off leaves?

1384
00:45:54,040 --> 00:45:55,059
Probably not.

1385
00:45:55,060 --> 00:45:56,279
Just rub it.

1386
00:45:56,280 --> 00:45:58,020
Yes, wash it whole.

1387
00:45:59,960 --> 00:46:01,180
Shouldn't tear it.

1388
00:46:03,340 --> 00:46:05,959
Are you stir‑frying cucumber?

1389
00:46:05,960 --> 00:46:07,920
Want some?

1390
00:46:14,380 --> 00:46:17,259
Have a cucumber.

1391
00:46:17,260 --> 00:46:18,719
Would you like to eat cucumber?

1392
00:46:18,720 --> 00:46:19,460
Raw?

1393
00:46:19,460 --> 00:46:20,100
Yes.

1394
00:46:20,100 --> 00:46:20,920
Here.

1395
00:46:20,920 --> 00:46:21,920
Do you want?

1396
00:46:21,921 --> 00:46:23,399
But you two already split it.

1397
00:46:23,400 --> 00:46:23,900
It's okay

1398
00:46:23,900 --> 00:46:24,640
three pieces.

1399
00:46:24,640 --> 00:46:25,480
Great.

1400
00:46:25,480 --> 00:46:26,480
Okay.

1401
00:46:28,120 --> 00:46:30,480
I mainly want cucumber.

1402
00:46:34,820 --> 00:46:35,919
Can someone cut it?

1403
00:46:35,920 --> 00:46:37,000
Cut it.

1404
00:46:38,860 --> 00:46:40,939
I'll help, let me.

1405
00:46:40,940 --> 00:46:42,339
I'll put it here.

1406
00:46:42,340 --> 00:46:43,340
Okay.

1407
00:46:43,600 --> 00:46:44,260
You're cutting outside.

1408
00:46:44,261 --> 00:46:45,539
Cut into small pieces?

1409
00:46:45,540 --> 00:46:47,339
Yes, small pieces.

1410
00:46:47,340 --> 00:46:48,340
Yes.

1411
00:46:54,000 --> 00:46:55,339
Can we catch that chicken

1412
00:46:55,340 --> 00:46:56,479
back home?

1413
00:46:56,480 --> 00:46:57,380
(Let's add another dish)
There's a chicken outside.

1414
00:46:57,381 --> 00:46:59,239
It's going home already.

1415
00:46:59,240 --> 00:47:01,120
But it's in the coop.

1416
00:47:02,740 --> 00:47:03,340
Rock‑paper‑scissors

1417
00:47:03,341 --> 00:47:04,420
loser washes dishes.

1418
00:47:08,260 --> 00:47:09,500
I'll sit for a bit.

1419
00:47:10,820 --> 00:47:13,000
Can it hold both of us?

1420
00:47:13,200 --> 00:47:15,200
(Chill)

1421
00:47:15,320 --> 00:47:16,619
The plates and bowls.

1422
00:47:16,620 --> 00:47:18,199
(Cozy)
I washed, and then

1423
00:47:18,200 --> 00:47:19,100
I sat down.

1424
00:47:19,101 --> 00:47:20,859
I couldn't help in the kitchen anymore,

1425
00:47:20,860 --> 00:47:22,859
and everything was clean.

1426
00:47:22,860 --> 00:47:23,999
So I just stayed out of the way

1427
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:25,439
and waited quietly.

1428
00:47:25,440 --> 00:47:27,239
While sitting in the
rocking chair, I thought

1429
00:47:27,240 --> 00:47:28,679
since I can't help much now

1430
00:47:28,680 --> 00:47:30,700
I'll just do the dishes later.

1431
00:47:36,580 --> 00:47:37,380
What's wrong?

1432
00:47:37,380 --> 00:47:38,320
Oh no, you cut yourself!

1433
00:47:38,320 --> 00:47:39,320
Who has a band‑aid?

1434
00:47:44,860 --> 00:47:46,720
Careful, that's a lot of blood.

1435
00:47:48,540 --> 00:47:49,739
I have band‑aids.

1436
00:47:49,740 --> 00:47:51,039
Use iodine first.

1437
00:47:51,040 --> 00:47:52,220
I have some.

1438
00:47:57,300 --> 00:47:58,399
Be careful.

1439
00:47:58,400 --> 00:47:59,600
That's a lot of blood.

1440
00:48:01,680 --> 00:48:02,600
Here, there is...

1441
00:48:02,600 --> 00:48:03,580
alcohol wipes.

1442
00:48:03,581 --> 00:48:04,599
Use an alcohol pad

1443
00:48:04,600 --> 00:48:06,159
disinfect first.

1444
00:48:06,160 --> 00:48:07,020
Oh my god.

1445
00:48:07,020 --> 00:48:08,020
Here.

1446
00:48:08,700 --> 00:48:10,499
That's a lot.

1447
00:48:10,500 --> 00:48:11,979
You cut deep into the flesh?

1448
00:48:11,980 --> 00:48:13,560
I think it's quite deep.

1449
00:48:25,660 --> 00:48:27,759
I was helping Elio cut green beans

1450
00:48:27,760 --> 00:48:29,659
for his stir‑fry.

1451
00:48:29,660 --> 00:48:30,699
And just like that,

1452
00:48:30,700 --> 00:48:32,459
I cut my thumb.

1453
00:48:32,460 --> 00:48:33,839
At that moment I thought.

1454
00:48:33,840 --> 00:48:36,480
Oh no.

1455
00:48:42,420 --> 00:48:43,420
It's okay, it's okay.

1456
00:48:45,780 --> 00:48:46,939
He's bleeding.

1457
00:48:46,940 --> 00:48:48,519
He really cut into the flesh

1458
00:48:48,520 --> 00:48:50,120
a lot of blood all over the floor.

1459
00:48:50,900 --> 00:48:52,600
Let me wipe it up first.

1460
00:48:53,560 --> 00:48:54,360
You can handle it yourself.

1461
00:48:54,360 --> 00:48:55,200
Here's a band‑aid

1462
00:48:55,200 --> 00:48:56,200
just stick it on.

1463
00:48:59,860 --> 00:49:01,980
I shouldn't have asked
him to cut the beans.

1464
00:49:02,940 --> 00:49:04,499
When I was just cooking

1465
00:49:04,500 --> 00:49:06,139
it was then that

1466
00:49:06,140 --> 00:49:07,799
I asked him to give me a hand

1467
00:49:07,800 --> 00:49:09,379
and then he cut himself

1468
00:49:09,380 --> 00:49:11,000
I feel guilty.

1469
00:49:18,140 --> 00:49:19,260
I've washed it.

1470
00:49:20,860 --> 00:49:22,360
Is it right?

1471
00:49:27,960 --> 00:49:28,520
Let me see.

1472
00:49:28,521 --> 00:49:29,660
Wait, OK.

1473
00:49:35,300 --> 00:49:36,359
Bandage.

1474
00:49:36,360 --> 00:49:37,640
I need some gauze.

1475
00:49:38,360 --> 00:49:39,400
Okay, that's it.

1476
00:49:40,200 --> 00:49:41,180
Clean up the floor.

1477
00:49:41,180 --> 00:49:41,880
So much blood.

1478
00:49:41,881 --> 00:49:43,140
I'll do it.

1479
00:49:48,120 --> 00:49:49,339
Does it still hurt?

1480
00:49:49,340 --> 00:49:51,299
I think you need a tetanus shot.

1481
00:49:51,300 --> 00:49:52,280
That cut looks deep, bleeding

1482
00:49:52,281 --> 00:49:54,160
and might need stitches.

1483
00:49:55,700 --> 00:49:57,200
(Next Episode)

1484
00:49:57,280 --> 00:49:58,320
Who?

1485
00:49:59,820 --> 00:50:01,220
Who is it?

1486
00:50:03,320 --> 00:50:05,519
It's a task box here.

1487
00:50:05,520 --> 00:50:07,039
Within 15 minutes,

1488
00:50:07,040 --> 00:50:11,960
write the name of the person you feel most
drawn to and why. Everyone only gets one vote.

